  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821136">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">nonlinear parameter estimation (Sips model)</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">nonlinear estimation of Sips isotherm parameters</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775715"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775716"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775770"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821135"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821138"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821139"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1684 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775714"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1684 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775767"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This task performs nonlinear parameter estimation using adsorption equilibrium data. The objective is to determine the Sips maximum adsorption capacity, the Sips equilibrium constant, and the Sips heterogeneity exponent by fitting the nonlinear Sips equation directly to measured solute concentrations and adsorbed amounts. The nonlinear approach preserves the combined Langmuir-Freundlich behavior of the model and avoids distortions introduced by linearization. The results characterize both the adsorption affinity and the degree of surface heterogeneity governing the adsorption process.</mathmoddb:P1459>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6820970">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q68663"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Kiselev isotherm model</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">adsorption model for localized monolayer with complex formation</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">The Kiselev isotherm model describes adsorption occurring in a localized monomolecular layer, where adsorbate molecules may form surface complexes with one another. Unlike the Langmuir model, Kiselev explicitly includes a complex-formation parameter that accounts for associations between adsorbed molecules at neighboring sites. This allows the model to represent cooperative or associative adsorption behavior on heterogeneous or interacting surfaces. It is used primarily to interpret adsorption on solids where pairwise interactions or dimer formation occurs. Applications include surface chemistry, catalysis, and environmental adsorption processes such as chemical wastewater treatment.</mathmoddb:P1459>
    <mathmoddb:P286 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775858"/>
    <mathmoddb:P147 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6820971"/>
