    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q60231"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">agronomy</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">science and technology of producing and using plants for food, fuel, fiber, and reclamation</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Agronomy is the science and technology of producing and using plants for food, fuel, fiber, and land management. A central concern of the discipline is the estimation and improvement of crop yield under field conditions. Agronomic models translate plant growth processes into practical measures of agricultural productivity. Harvest index–based approaches provide a widely used method to link biomass production with economically relevant yield.</mathmoddb:P1459>
