  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775503">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">light particle propagation</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">propagating the (quantum!) state of the light particle(s) in quantum-classical dynamics models</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P1690 rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mixed_quantum-classical_dynamics"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1690 rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q65091550"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775478"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Note that in quantum-classical dynamics the effective Hamiltonian governing the quantum dynamics of the light particles parametrically depends on the heavy particle(s) positions.</mathmoddb:P1459>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">The electrons are usually treated by a local approximation of the TDSE, i.e., they depend only on the electronic forces and couplings at the instantaneous position of the nuclei.</mathmoddb:P1459>
  </rdf:Description>
