    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">uni uni reaction with competitive complete inhibition</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">uni uni reaction with inhibition</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Enzyme (E) and Substrate (S) form an enzyme-substrate complex (ES), which catalyzes the formation of product (P). Rates for complex formation and dissociation are k₁ and k₋₁, k₂ is the rate of the rate-determining enzymatic step of product formation. Free enzyme may bind an inhibitor (I) to form an enzyme-inhibitor complex (EI) with rates k₃ and k₋₃.</mathmoddb:P1459>
