  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821388">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">computation of rooting depth</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">calculates crop rooting depth from phenological development</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This task computes crop rooting depth as a function of phenological development and crop-specific root characteristics. Rooting depth increases with accumulated heat units and is capped by the potential root zone depth of the soil. The task produces a deterministic estimate of rooting depth at each time step. The resulting depth constrains root biomass distribution and soil water and nutrient uptake processes.</mathmoddb:P1459>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821272"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821277"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821380"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821381"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821382"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821385"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821386"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821187">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q68663"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Fritz-Schlunder 4-parameter isotherm model</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">flexible four-parameter empirical adsorption isotherm</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P286 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775858"/>
    <mathmoddb:P286 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821201"/>
    <mathmoddb:P147 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821190"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821188"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821189"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534270"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">The Fritz-Schlunder 4-parameter isotherm model is an empirical equation providing high flexibility for modeling adsorption on heterogeneous surfaces. It introduces two independent exponents and two affinity parameters, enabling extremely close fits to non-ideal adsorption data over wide concentration ranges. Because of its general form, the model does not assume monolayer behavior and imposes no strict physical interpretation on its parameters. It is especially useful when typical three-parameter models fail to capture complex curvature in experimental isotherms. Applications include chemical wastewater treatment, dye removal, heavy metals removal, and adsorption process design.</mathmoddb:P1459>
    <mathmoddb:P1684 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775713"/>
    <mathmoddb:P1684 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775766"/>
  </rdf:Description>
